What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../link_state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only MT6580 firmware PWRAP link diagnostics. Reading the
		attribute performs one serialized, side-effect-free MT6350 DEW
		read test at 0x018c, expecting 0x5aa5. It never resets the bus,
		recalibrates timing, or retries a failed PMIC command.

		init_done and wacs2 report a current raw WACS2 status snapshot.
		read_test/error report the last test result; checks/failures
		count tests since probe. Counters wrap at 32 bits. reads/writes
		count attempted transactions, including failures and read tests.
		errors/timeouts/init_lost count transport failures, timeout
		failures, and failures with INIT_DONE absent. stale_valid_clears
		counts acknowledgements of VALID seen before a new command;
		it does not prove that every acknowledgement followed a timeout.

		last_error/reg/write/stage/status retain the latest failed
		transport operation even after later successes. Stage 0 waits
		for idle before issuing a command, stage 1 waits for a read
		result, and stage 2 waits for write completion. With no recorded
		failure these fields are zero. A signature mismatch increments
		test failures, not transport errors.

		Counters and the saved failure are snapshotted under a spinlock;
		the live WACS2 status is sampled separately and can change as
		other PMIC users run. The attribute makes no cold-initialization
		or destructive-recovery capability available to userspace.
